R-CM11 R-LB2 R-FL14 R-LD4 R-LD6 R-LD7 R-BL1 R-BL5 R-P6 R-PH10 R-PH13 R-EC10 R-EC11 R-PD9 R-SO7 R-PH8 R-SE7 R-CC2 R-PP3 R-P1 R-SE4 R-SP2 R-RP2 (slice 009, Q4, Q7): the command code of `verify` with the fake Fx, 5 runs on 5 projects (all in one dir with a `.git`).
The calls of one run fix the order of Verify.run!: args, env, clock, cwd, the project, canonical and the record in projects.json, `programs` and `roc version`, `read_files` of the member file and the talon.toml candidate, the index and the package headers (the tuple of `update`), then the ladder with no copy: `random`, `make_dirs` of a temp dir (it holds the output of the build only), one round of probes (the baseline and the candidate check, both in the project dir, the candidate with one `--replace-dep <old> <new>` for each entry that differs), the build (an app only, in the project dir, with the same flags and the output in the temp dir) and `delete` of the temp dir. There is no `copy_tree`, no second read and no `write_atomic` of a project file (R-CM11: it writes nothing).
Run 1 (v1, an app with no `roc:` pin): the tuple moves json, parser and the platform: the notice R-SE7, the ladder lines, the plan (`~` lines, and no `+ roc:` line: verify writes no pin, R-H6, R-RP3) and the last line. Run 2 (v2, a package `lib/main.roc`): 2 probes, no build (R-LD7). Run 3 (v3): the candidate has a new error in the files of acme/json 2.1.0: exit 10 (R-PH10, R-PH13). The text of the check output has the paths of a check that runs in the project dir (`probe-pkg-new.stderr`). Run 4 (v4): a new error in an app file: exit 11. In runs 3 and 4 the temp dir is deleted (R-CC2) and nothing is written.
Run 5 (v5): the header is the tuple (the newest release in range). Q4: the ladder still runs: 3 probes, and the candidate check has no `--replace-dep`.
